<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Reserve Bank of Australia commodity index up.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Reserve Bank of Australia commodity index up.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of Australia said its index of commodity prices rose by 1.4 percent in Special Drawing Rights (SDR) terms in February, matching January's rise.</p>
<p>Rises in the prices of wool, beef and base metals were partly offset by a fall in the price of crude oil, the bank said.</p>
<p>In Australian dollar terms, the index rose by 0.4 percent in February after a 2.5 percent rise in January.</p>
<p>The Reserve Bank indices were as follows (base 1989/90):  </p>
<p>		     All Items		    Rural Component</p>
<p>		A$	SDR	US$	   A$	SDR	US$</p>
<p>Feb 97 p  92.2     85.7     91.9	 84.4     78.4     84.1</p>
<p>Jan 97 r  91.8     84.5     92.9	 82.1     75.6     83.1</p>
<p>Feb 96    96.5     83.5     94.7	 87.0     75.3     85.3</p>
<p>		 Non-Rural Component     of which: Base Metals</p>
<p>		A$	SDR	US$	  A$	 SDR	US$</p>
<p>Feb 97 p  97.0     90.1     96.7	91.0	84.5     90.8</p>
<p>Jan 97 r  97.8     90.0     98.9	88.5	81.4     89.6</p>
<p>Feb 96   101.7     88.0     99.8	94.8	81.9     93.0</p>
<p>NOTE - r = revised, p = preliminary</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
